  "body": "Found by the review of PR 1435 (Mazak spindle words), as a note outside that PR's scope: in `assets/posts/mazak.cps` a tapping cycle is posted as `G84` with the spindle started `M3`, whatever the tap's hand. For a left-hand tap that is the wrong direction and the wrong cycle (ISO/Fanuc-family controls use `G74` with `M4` for left-hand tapping). The behaviour is older than PR 1435; that PR did not change it.\n\nTo settle first: can a left-hand tap be set up today (a tool or operation parameter for thread hand)? If it cannot, the defect is unreachable and this becomes \"refuse or support left-hand tapping\" for every post; if it can, a left-hand tap posts a program that would break the tap or strip the thread.\n\nWanted: every post either writes the left-hand cycle and spindle direction correctly for its dialect or refuses a left-hand tap by name. Check the other posts for the same assumption, not only Mazak.\n\nSources: RS-274 / ISO 6983 and the project's own posts only. Not exercised on a real control.\n\nDone means: a test posts a left-hand tap on Mazak (and each post that claims tapping) and gets either the left-hand cycle with reverse spindle or a named refusal; a right-hand tap's golden is unchanged.\n",
